# Echo: A Social Community Board

### Project Narrative
You are going to build Echo, a clean and fast social board where people can share ideas. You will start by setting up your project and creating a simple list of topics. Then, you will build a database to store every post forever. You will add a way for users to sign up and log in so they can join the conversation. Finally, you will add a comment section so users can reply to each other and keep the discussion going.

### Story Arc
Meet Sarah. She is a massive fan of retro video games, but she is tired of the big social media sites. Every time she tries to find a group for her favorite classic game, her feed is filled with ads, random videos, and people arguing about things that have nothing to do with gaming. It is too noisy and she just wants a quiet corner of the internet to talk about high scores.

Sarah wants a place where she can post a topic and have a real conversation without all the extra clutter. She has a vision for a site called Echo, but right now, she only has a few drawings in her notebook. She needs a way to make the site work so people can actually type their thoughts and see them appear on the screen.

That is where you come in. You are going to build the engine that powers Echo. You will create the pages, set up the user accounts, and build the system that lets Sarah and her friends talk to each other. By the time you are done, Sarah will finally have the perfect digital clubhouse for her community. Let us get started.

